{"id":"c1d30833f43eecf0","group":"62","path":"62/62-thm-ACA0-vector-basis.md","title":"ACA0 and Bases of Countable Vector Spaces","display":"thm-ACA0-vector-basis — ACA0 and Bases of Countable Vector Spaces","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Subsystems of Second Order Arithmetic (Simpson)","book_abbrev":"62","label":"62-thm-ACA0-vector-basis","aliases":["62-thm-ACA0-vector-basis"],"display":"thm-ACA0-vector-basis — ACA0 and Bases of Countable Vector Spaces","depends_on":["[[62-df-RCA0]]","[[62-df-ACA0]]","[[62-df-vector-basis-principles]]","[[62-df-equivalence-over-base]]","[[62-thm-ACA0-equivalences]]"],"source":"Simpson, 2nd edition (2009), Lemma III.4.2; Theorem III.4.3","source_pages":[112,113],"source_pdf_pages":[130,131]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Subsystems of Second Order Arithmetic (Simpson)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"62"},{"key":"label","html":"62-thm-ACA0-vector-basis"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>62-thm-ACA0-vector-basis</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-ACA0-vector-basis — ACA0 and Bases of Countable Vector Spaces"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"dd5e8930337c8b20\" href=\"?note=dd5e8930337c8b20\" title=\"62-df-RCA0\">62-df-RCA0</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"35af454d9caa8c9d\" href=\"?note=35af454d9caa8c9d\" title=\"62-df-ACA0\">62-df-ACA0</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"752a37b813c0e71e\" href=\"?note=752a37b813c0e71e\" title=\"62-df-vector-basis-principles\">62-df-vector-basis-principles</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"781620ab41bfeebd\" href=\"?note=781620ab41bfeebd\" title=\"62-df-equivalence-over-base\">62-df-equivalence-over-base</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"eddcc3574973d5b4\" href=\"?note=eddcc3574973d5b4\" title=\"62-thm-ACA0-equivalences\">62-thm-ACA0-equivalences</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source","html":"Simpson, 2nd edition (2009), Lemma III.4.2; Theorem III.4.3"},{"key":"source_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>112</span><span>113</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>130</span><span>131</span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RCA}_0,\\mathrm{ACA}_0\">\\(\\mathrm{RCA}_0,\\mathrm{ACA}_0\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"dd5e8930337c8b20\" href=\"?note=dd5e8930337c8b20\" title=\"62-df-RCA0\">62-df-RCA0</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"35af454d9caa8c9d\" href=\"?note=35af454d9caa8c9d\" title=\"62-df-ACA0\">62-df-ACA0</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{VB},\\mathrm{VBQ}\">\\(\\mathrm{VB},\\mathrm{VBQ}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"752a37b813c0e71e\" href=\"?note=752a37b813c0e71e\" title=\"62-df-vector-basis-principles\">62-df-vector-basis-principles</a>，EquivOver 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"781620ab41bfeebd\" href=\"?note=781620ab41bfeebd\" title=\"62-df-equivalence-over-base\">62-df-equivalence-over-base</a>；反向以 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"eddcc3574973d5b4\" href=\"?note=eddcc3574973d5b4\" title=\"62-thm-ACA0-equivalences\">62-thm-ACA0-equivalences</a> 的单射值域原则为目标。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ACA0\\text{-}vector\\text{-}basis}\\vdash\\;\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\mathrm{ACA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{VB}\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0),\\\\\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\mathrm{ACA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{VBQ}\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ACA0\\text{-}vector\\text{-}basis}\\vdash\\;\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\mathrm{ACA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{VB}\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0),\\\\\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\mathrm{ACA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{VBQ}\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>正向用算术理解形成“末向量在前面有限向量张成中”的数码集合，再按数码顺序贪心选择向量。若递归有限终止，所得有限集合是基；否则 ACA₀ 形成其值域作为基。零空间在空基处终止，不能强求无限基列。</p>\n<p>反向依 III.4.3。对单射 f，令有理自由向量空间 V₀ 的基为 xₙ，取 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x&#39;_m=x_{2f(m)}+m\\,x_{2f(m)+1}\">\\(x&#39;_m=x_{2f(m)}+m\\,x_{2f(m)+1}\\)</span>。张成这些向量的 U 可由每个有限支撑的系数比值检验而在 RCA₀ 中形成；按 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v-w\\in U\">\\(v-w\\in U\\)</span> 的最小数码代表构造 V₀/U。该商的一个基提升后，与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x&#39;_m\">\\(x&#39;_m\\)</span> 一起成为 V₀ 的基；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x_{2n}\">\\(x_{2n}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x_{2n+1}\">\\(x_{2n+1}\\)</span> 的唯一有限支撑表示判断 n 是否属于 f 的值域，Δ⁰₁ 理解恢复这个集合。不是对没有已给基的一般空间直接使用消元来判定所有独立性。</p>\n<p>来源：第二版（2009），Lemma III.4.2; Theorem III.4.3；纸面页 112, 113；PDF 页 130, 131。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"62-df-RCA0","status":"resolved","id":"dd5e8930337c8b20","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[62-df-RCA0]]","embed":false},{"target":"62-df-ACA0","status":"resolved","id":"35af454d9caa8c9d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[62-df-ACA0]]","embed":false},{"target":"62-df-vector-basis-principles","status":"resolved","id":"752a37b813c0e71e","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[62-df-vector-basis-principles]]","embed":false},{"target":"62-df-equivalence-over-base","status":"resolved","id":"781620ab41bfeebd","ancho